 "surplus_use": {
  "what": "Where the year-end operating surplus goes, in the City's own words (Annual Financial Reports).",
  "rows": [
   {
    "fact": "The operating fund variance (the year-end operating surplus) is transferred to the Fiscal Stability Reserve (FSR) in the next fiscal year: $236 million for 2023, $276 million for 2024 and $259 million for 2025.",
    "source": "afr2025",
    "pdf_page": 24,
    "printed_page": 22,
    "also": {
     "source": "afr2024",
     "pdf_page": 29,
     "printed_page": 27
    }
   },
   {
    "fact": "The FSR is a contingency fund for operational emergencies, urgent or contingency capital spending, and unplanned drops in revenue with significant financial impact; investment income from the reserve can fund one-time operating spending.",
    "source": "afr2025",
    "pdf_page": 24,
    "printed_page": 22
   },
   {
    "fact": "The FSR held $1,214 million at the end of 2024 and $1,353 million at the end of 2025, each including that year's operating surplus.",
    "source": "afr2025",
    "pdf_page": 25,
    "printed_page": 23
   },
   {
    "year": "2023",
    "fact": "In November 2023 (C2023-1148) Council approved a draw of $88 million from the FSR for new one-time operating and capital investments, and a further $100 million for new capital investments from the anticipated 2023 operating surplus flowing through the FSR. A $242 million contribution was also transferred from the FSR to the Major capital projects reserve (C2023-0482).",
    "source": "afr2023",
    "pdf_page": 30,
    "printed_page": 28
   },
   {
    "year": "2024",
    "fact": "In November 2024 (C2024-1097) Council approved a draw of $61 million from the FSR for new one-time operating and capital investments. A $136 million contribution was transferred from the FSR to the capital and lifecycle reserve (RFC/LMUR, C2024-0552).",
    "source": "afr2024",
    "pdf_page": 30,
    "printed_page": 28,
    "also": {
     "source": "afr2024",
     "pdf_page": 29,
     "printed_page": 27
    }
   },
   {
    "year": "2025",
    "fact": "In November 2025 (C2025-0901) Council approved a draw of $317 million from the FSR for new one-time operating and capital investments and contributions to the Heritage Incentive Reserve and the Heritage Calgary Reserve fund. A $15 million contribution was transferred from the FSR to the Opportunity Calgary Investment Fund (EC2025-0406).",
    "source": "afr2025",
    "pdf_page": 25,
    "printed_page": 23
   }
  ],
  "limits": "The reports do not tie a particular year's surplus to a particular later spending decision or to property tax relief; the surplus joins the reserve balance, and Council approves draws from the reserve. Years before 2023 are not read here."
 },
